  "lesson": "## Play the pads as notes\n\nHot cue 1 on a single sustained note or stab, KEY SHIFT mode on the pads so each pad retriggers that cue at a different pitch. The drill plays a simple two-bar melody: two notes each on pads 4, 6 and 7, then down through 5, 4, 3 to 2, one press per beat.\n\nTone play turns one sample into an instrument, and it is scored like drumming: the press has to be on the beat. The musical part is choosing the source: a clean, short sound with a clear pitch. Which pad is which pitch depends on your software's key shift layout, so learn it before the melody, and turn the audio on for this one.\n",
